AB  - Large Language Models (LLMs) are now being used in complex, interconnected systems-where several models and retrieval tools work together across different services. But debugging these pipelines isn't easy. When something goes wrong, it's usually not a clear-cut error message or crash. Instead, problems show up as subtle semantic issues: hallucinated facts, drifting prompts, or unpredictable reasoning paths that are hard to trace or reproduce. To address this, we introduce Panopticon-a distributed observability framework designed to make LLM-based applications more transparent and easier to debug. Panopticon combines semantic provenance tracing with LLM-assisted analysis to automatically spot issues. We tested Panopticon on a retrieval-augmented question-answering pipeline (HotpotQA) and found that it could systematically detect semantic anomalies in about 1 2. 4% of cases-without hurting overall performance.
ER  - 

