AB  - While a plethora of deep learning (DL) models exist, there is hardly any verifiable DL code that can be executed on public blockchains. In this paper, we propose approach named as PSTL (PyTorch to Solidity code Translation using LLMs) for translating code of DL models like Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) to Solidity deployment on Ethereum blockchain. Extensive prompt engineering to achieve gas cost optimization of the produced Solidity code. We also incorporate Retrieval Augmented Generation to improve the quality of the translated code. Additionally, we introduce an enhanced evaluation metric by extending CodeBERTScore for Solidity. We have also built a decentralized application (dApp) to showcase how the accuracy of CNN models can be verified on the Ethereum test network.
